## Deck-wide defaults

`defaults` in `deck.json` is a `<slide>` block applied to **every** slide; `columns` is the same for slides that show two columns and `textOnly` for slides without code. A slide's own settings win.

<code lang=jsonc>
  "defaults": {
    "justify": "true",
    "padding": "9vmin 12vmin",
    "heading-size": "56"
  },
  "columns": {
    "valign": "center"
  },
  "textOnly": {
    "halign": "center",
    "valign": "center"
  }
</code>

Together with `themes`, `vars`, `header`/`footer` and `css` it is enough to build a house style once and
reuse it for every deck of a school or company.

<notes>
  Defaults accept any key a slide accepts: layout, theme, background, transition, --variables.
</notes>
